WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.880
So, as kids we used to wander through here and wander through the buildings

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:15.340
and when we were, I would say
maybe 12 years old or so, a bunch of us were invited ...

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.340
We had a scoutmaster who
graduated from MIT and had an

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:25.439
affiliation and he got us, one night a
week, into the MIT swimming pool, which to me

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:30.739
was unbelievable. So I just saw this swimming pool back then

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:34.860
in the late fifties and I couldn't
believe that, you know, kids like us

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.270
would have the opportunity to go to a
building like that. And then there were

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:43.400
MIT students that used to volunteer, come to the Boy Scout meetings and help teach us

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:48.500
things about camping and physical
fitness. And it was sort of a connection.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.440
So that's the early connection I had.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:59.380
MIT used to sponsor our Boy Scout Troop. I was a Boy Scout.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:07.800
It was Troop 77 and it was in building 20 maybe? On Vassar Street.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:16.540
We used to meet there. Troop 77, and that was my first experience with Boy Scouts.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.920
It was a great experience. Our scout master was Mr. Lambert,

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:32.540
MIT donated the facilities, so we used to get to go in, have our scout meetings and everything ...

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:42.800
The Boy Scouts oath is "On my honor I will do my best to 
do my duty to God and country,

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:50.460
I will obey the Scout law.  I will help other people at all times.  I will keep myself

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:56.220
physically strong, mentally awake, and morally straight.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:03.420
That's a wonderful thing, I've never I've never forgotten it. I learned it as a kid,

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.429
I learned it at Troop 77, MIT building 20.

